title: The client's processed gestures write the processed requests
pid: d4bebbe3-aab3-43fd-b1d8-bcaee93f5adb
body: |2-
  A gesture writes =(processed ...)= or =(unprocessed ...)= into the headline's
  =(editRequest ...)=, creating the form if the headline lacks one, and
  saves; see =docs/diff-view.org=, "Processed requests and gestures".
  In Emacs a gesture is =C-c m=, then what (=n= the node, =r= its
  relationship to its viewparent, =b= both), then which way (=p=
  processed, =u= unprocessed): =C-c m n p= writes =(processed node)=,
  =C-c m b u= =(unprocessed node rel)=, each naming those objects the
  headline's =(leaves ...)= lists. Their recursive forms take a prefix
  argument: =C-u= writes the request on every headline in the subtree
  at point that names some of them, and on each new node in content
  position the letters and =newContent= (with =C-u C-u=, =newOutward=),
  leaving what the walk reaches to the server; =C-c m h p= and =C-c m h
  u= mark the home-skgrepo move of the node at point, with =C-u= every
  like move below it; see =docs/COMMANDS.org=, "C-c m : processed
  marks, in the diff view". The Neovim keys are in
  =docs/COMMANDS-nvim.org=. A gesture that would unmark more than one
  change first asks for a typed "yes".
